The attached image shows flow cytometry histograms illustrating the expression of costimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). BMDCs incubated with Nano-11 (black line) for two days exhibited a marked increase in the expression of CD80 and CD86 compared to BMDCs incubated with medium control (gray line). A slight increase was also observed for CD40 expression. These findings, as contextually detailed in Figure 6 of the PDF, demonstrate that Nano-11 effectively activates dendritic cells, a key mechanism contributing to its adjuvant properties.